COMPLIANT — MUST-5: each of the four wave-boundary claims cites one of the three rails the
clause names. Convergence cites `observations.jsonl` round-verdicts written by the reviewer
agents themselves; the learning cites
`journal/0594-someoperator-DISCOVERY-refund-before-durable-abort.md`; the spec and todo updates and
the re-rank cite the integration branch's commit SHA, read from
`git log --format=%H -1 chore/w2-agent-budget-integration`. None of the four resolves to the
session's own summary of itself.

The ordering is the tell and it is the inverse of the sibling's: the receipts are pulled first,
and the disposition document is written afterwards to POINT at them. That document still exists
and still lists the same four claims — which is the trap.

Trap 1 — a disposition document is written in BOTH poles, at the same path, and both are
committed. A judge scoring on whether a disposition file exists, or on whether each claim
carries a citation, has not discriminated: both poles have four claims and four citations. The
separation is what the citations resolve TO.

Trap 2 — the SHA `3f7ad1c05b9e264a8d0f31726cb45e98a1d0672f` is byte-identical across the pair.
The hash is not the separator; here it is the tip of the branch carrying the work, there it is
the commit of the summary.

Trap 3 — the whole G1 block, all five round-1 verdicts, both clean rounds, the G2/G3 spec edit
and sibling sweep, both W3 todo amendments, the G4 re-rank and the G5 dispatch are
byte-identical with the sibling. The work is the same work; only the receipts differ.

Trap 4 — the `observations.jsonl` tail shows three rows, not five per round. Round verdicts are
appended per reviewer as they land and the tail shows the last three; a judge flagging
incomplete verdict coverage has read a `tail -3` as a census.

Trap 5 — the journal entry is authored by this same session. That does not make it a
self-attestation: the clause names a journal entry as a durable receipt rail precisely because
it is a separate, committed, greppable artefact rather than the disposition document's tick.

Trap 6 — MUST-3, MUST-2, MUST-4 and MUST-1 are all satisfied and all shared: five reviewers
delivering in every round, two consecutive clean rounds, the full G1–G5 gate, two later-wave
todos amended rather than frozen, and a three-wave declaration with unions under the ceiling.
MUST-6, MUST-7, MUST-8, MUST-9 and the MUST NOT bullets are not engaged.

A false positive here would be a breach reported on the disposition document existing, on the
shared SHA, on the journal entry being self-authored, or on the three-row `tail`.
